<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  "حسابي" — the account information card, EDIT state. Figma 562:17237.

  ===========================================================================
  WHY THE EDIT STATE IS A SECOND URL AND NOT AN INLINE TOGGLE
  ===========================================================================
  Figma draws two frames: 562:10229 (values, one تعديل button) and 562:17237
  (the same card with inputs and حفظ التغييرات / الغاء). The obvious reading is
  an in-place toggle, and it is the wrong one to build.

  Two server-rendered states at two URLs cost ZERO JavaScript, work with the
  browser's own back button, survive a failed save with Magento's own message
  block and repopulated form, and put the change-email/change-password
  machinery on the page Magento already validates it on. An inline toggle would
  need a script to swap the states, a second script to post them, and its own
  answer to "what does back do" — for a visual result the shopper cannot
  distinguish from a page load on this card.

  It is also what the rest of this section already does: تعديل on an address
  card goes to the address form, not into the card.

  The block, its name and its cacheable flag are core's; only the template and
  the injected view models change.
-->
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <body>
        <referenceBlock name="customer_edit">
            <arguments>
                <!--
                  Both, and they are not redundant. Profile answers "what should
                  this card print" (and applies the placeholder rule itself);
                  CustomerEmail answers "is the STORED value a placeholder",
                  which core's change-email fieldset needs in order to decide
                  between "add" and "change" wording and whether to put the
                  stored address in a value attribute at all.
                -->
                <argument name="profile" xsi:type="object">Spartrak\CustomerAccount\ViewModel\Profile</argument>
                <argument name="customer_email" xsi:type="object">Spartrak\CustomerAuth\ViewModel\CustomerEmail</argument>
                <!--
                  The OTP dialog on this card (Figma 1078:7263) renders one box
                  per digit and re-sends on a cooldown, both of which are
                  admin-configurable. Read from the SAME view model the login
                  modal reads (Magento_Theme::html/login-modal.phtml), so a
                  merchant changing the code length changes it in both places
                  and cannot end up with a four-box dialog verifying a six-digit
                  code.
                -->
                <argument name="auth_config" xsi:type="object">Spartrak\CustomerAuth\ViewModel\AuthConfig</argument>
            </arguments>
        </referenceBlock>
    </body>
</page>
